<p class="tk-prose__lead">In force since 17 September 2026. First edition.</p>

<h3>1. Who processes your data</h3>
<p>Personal data of Takebana users (takebana.com) is processed by Murat Kunizhev, Republic of Serbia. For questions about data and for requests about your rights, write to <a href="mailto:private@takebana.com">private@takebana.com</a>.</p>
<p>This policy follows the EU General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR), the Serbian Personal Data Protection Act, and the California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA/CPRA).</p>

<h3>2. What we collect</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Account:</strong> email address, name (login), password stored as an irreversible hash, profile photo and personal gallery, the 18+ confirmation flag, and the sign-in method (password or Google).</li>
<li><strong>Content you create:</strong> streams and their settings, stream recordings, cover images, direct messages, stream chat messages, reports, ratings, subscriptions.</li>
<li><strong>Calls:</strong> who called whom, when, how long it lasted and how it ended. We do not record or store the conversation itself.</li>
<li><strong>Venues:</strong> name, type, country, city, address, map point, phone, email, opening hours, photos.</li>
<li><strong>Technical records:</strong> IP address and browser details in the action log and the error log, and the times of sign-ins and actions.</li>
</ul>
<p>We do not collect data about health, beliefs, religion or other special categories, and we do not ask you for them. We run no analytics, no advertising pixels and no cross-site tracking.</p>

<h3>3. Why, and on what legal basis</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>To run the platform</strong> — sign-in, streams, calls, messages, the venue map. Basis: performance of our contract with you.</li>
<li><strong>Security and handling abuse</strong> — action and error logs, reports, account restrictions. Basis: our legitimate interest in protecting users and the platform.</li>
<li><strong>Service email</strong> — password recovery. Basis: performance of the contract.</li>
<li><strong>Meeting legal duties</strong> — answering lawful requests from authorities. Basis: legal obligation.</li>
</ul>
<p>We send no marketing email.</p>

<h3>4. Who we share data with</h3>
<p>We do not sell data and do not give it to advertisers. Data reaches only the contractors the platform needs to work:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Daily (Pluot Inc., USA)</strong> — video calling: calls, venue cameras and the host side of a browser stream. Receives your device address and the audio and video during a conversation.</li>
<li><strong>Bunny (BunnyWay d.o.o., Slovenia)</strong> — storage of stream recordings and delivery of video to viewers. Receives the viewer’s device address.</li>
<li><strong>Google (Google Ireland Ltd.)</strong> — Google sign-in only, if you use it. We receive your email address and profile identifier from Google.</li>
<li><strong>Resend (USA, sending from the São Paulo region, Brazil)</strong> — platform email, such as a password recovery link. Receives your email address and the message.</li>
<li><strong>Hostinger (Lithuania)</strong> — the server the platform runs on, holding the database.</li>
<li><strong>Cloudflare (USA)</strong> — the domain’s DNS records and forwarding of mail sent to <code>@takebana.com</code> addresses to the platform’s working mailbox.</li>
<li><strong>OpenStreetMap (Nominatim)</strong> — looking up coordinates for a venue address. Only the address text is sent, with nothing about the user, and the request is made by our server, not your browser.</li>
</ul>
<p>Transfers outside the EU (Daily, Resend, Cloudflare) rely on the European Commission’s standard contractual clauses. We also disclose data on a lawful order of a court or authority, and we report child sexual exploitation material to law enforcement.</p>

<h3>5. Where data is stored</h3>
<p>The platform server and the database are in the European Union. Stream recordings are stored in Bunny’s European storage. Database backups are kept on the same server.</p>

<h3>6. How long we keep it</h3>
<ul>
<li>The account and its content — while the account exists.</li>
<li>Stream recordings — until the author deletes them.</li>
<li>Action log, including IP addresses — 180 days, then deleted automatically.</li>
<li>Error log — 90 days, then deleted automatically.</li>
<li>Sign-in session — 7 days from the last visit.</li>
<li>Password recovery link — one hour and a single use.</li>
</ul>
<p>When an account is deleted, its content goes at once. Entries about the deletion itself and about earlier actions stay in the action log until its retention period ends: they are needed for disputes and abuse handling.</p>

<h3>7. Your rights</h3>
<p>You may: get a copy of your data; correct inaccurate data; have data deleted; restrict processing; object to processing based on our legitimate interest; receive your data in a machine-readable form; and withdraw consent where processing is based on it.</p>
<p>Much of this is done in your account: name, photo and gallery in Settings, streams and recordings on your page, and the whole account with the “Delete account” button in Settings.</p>
<p>For anything else, write to <a href="mailto:private@takebana.com">private@takebana.com</a>. We answer within 30 days. If our answer does not satisfy you, you may complain to a supervisory authority: in Serbia, the Commissioner for Information of Public Importance and Personal Data Protection; in the EU, the authority of your country.</p>

<h3>8. For California residents</h3>
<p>Over the past 12 months we collected the categories listed in section 2: identifiers (email, name), device and connection details (IP address, browser), the content you create, and information about your use of the platform. The source is you and your device. The purposes are in section 3.</p>
<p><strong>We do not sell personal information and do not share it for targeted advertising</strong> — neither for money nor otherwise. We do not use sensitive information to infer characteristics about you.</p>
<p>You have the right to know what data we hold about you, to request its deletion or correction, and not to be discriminated against for exercising these rights. Send requests to the same address. An authorised agent may act for you with proof of authorisation.</p>

<h3>9. Children</h3>
<p>The platform is intended for people over 18. We do not knowingly collect children’s data. If you know that a child has an account here, write to us and we will delete the account and the data.</p>

<h3>10. Security</h3>
<p>Passwords are stored as irreversible hashes. The site runs over HTTPS. Access to the server and the database is limited to a small number of people. Administrator actions are written to a log. No system is perfectly secure, and we cannot promise absolute safety.</p>

<h3>11. Changes</h3>
<p>A new edition takes effect on the date at the top of this page. We will announce significant changes on the site.</p>
